{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1410967-splat-pitch-long-term-hobby","id":1410967,"title":"Splat Pitch. Long term hobby.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-29T00:55:07-07:00","id":1410967,"title":"Splat Pitch. Long term hobby.","content":"Over the years I have come up with several homebrew games for my players and amongst ourselves we have had quite a bit of fun. After a few years of doing this I want to make a game based off of concepts that my players and I have always wanted to try together, and this go around I want to make the best homebrew game I can.<br /> <br /> Ideas so far for my monster game:<br /> <br /> 1) The basic premise for this game is that you play a seemingly regular person that one day expresses monstrous traits and powers due to genes you possess passed down by an ancient monster that manipulated your family line. This monstrous ancestor was one of the Cthulhi that escaped R'lyeh shortly before or shortly after it began to sink into the ocean. The question I must think through here is did one escape and proliferate, or did 5 escape leading to 5 bloodlines? CofD seems to lean towards having groups of 5. And where did these beings go?<br /> <br /> 2) What powers did you get? My thoughts would be to have psychic abilities (not the merits but actual powers tooled for the Cthulhi) and some form of ritual magic. Mental discipline and mastery would be one side of the coin, dark occult rites would be the other side. I have thought of maybe running these two abilities off two &quot;morality equivalents&quot; like...Stability for psychic abilities and Sanity for rites. I like the idea of risking sanity to learn occult machinations and running the risk of your mind powers backfiring or overloading due to instability. <br /> <br /> 3) How strange are you? Your body starts to take on traits similar to the foreign matter of the spawn. You regenerate because like the old ones before you, your mind maintains your body not the other way around. You have mental powers (not that strange in CofD), and you have the ability to shapeshift between a myriad of forms. Primarily human (maybe able to assume multiple personas) Hybrid (illithid-esque), Octopus/squid, and small god. Each would have its benefits/drawbacks...but eh I'm not there yet.<br /> <br /> 4) Items? In lovecraftian fiction there are a plethora of objects made from unearthly alloys and foreign heavy stone. Perhaps a balance of sci-fi exotica grounded with old world dark sinister overtones? <br /> <br /> 5) Here comes the big idea...this is not meant for crossover games. All other supernaturals are enemies/resources/myths/monsters. In this shard of the world of darkness the Mythos supercedes the lore of these other groups. They only think they know.<br /> -Vampires are nesting monsters that ape at human and look down on their betters.<br /> -Werewolves may be shamans while human but on their phase of the moon they assume 1 of their wolf forms exclusively and become the animal. They pray to Luna, but is she really a spirit?<br /> -Demons/Angels are unknowable and utterly inhuman. How do you reason with something that has no common ground? Could be that their God is nothing but an alien AI that has outlived it's purpose.<br /> -Changelings hide. It's what they do. You ignore the ones that just want to be left alone, keep an eye out for power hungry tyrants, and always watch out for whatever alien-born menace they might attract or call up.<br /> -Mummies...possible cult leaders so this dynamic could be friend or foe all depending. Ill think more on this.<br /> <br /> <br /> 6) Quick ideas:<br /> -Power stat= Mythos. As mythos increases so do the normal aspects along with regeneration and...maybe some perception mechanic.<br /> -Morality Analogue= Stability and Sanity.<br /> -Fuel Stat= Not sure yet<br /> <br /> That's what I got after about 10 minutes of brainstorming. I eventually want to do a complete write up on this. Everyone needs a hobby. Any suggestions?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T07:34:48-07:00","id":1410994,"title":"","content":"Interesting hmmm, what influence beyond the Mythos do you think would be appropriate inspiration?<br /> <br /> I'm a fan of the Yellow Sign and the King in Yellow. What are you thoughts on R'lyeh and other weird places like Carcosa existing. Would you think they are places that you could visit, like going to the Hedge, or would they be more mythical hard to reach places like Arcadia? Maybe such places exist as individual Lower Depth Realms?<br /> <br /> The Fan Gameline Leviathan kind of touched a little bit into this theme. And what are the general goals? Will they be unified, or will they be divided into factions like those wanting to enslave the world for the Old Ones or those fighting to keep them asleep and unaware, or even Factions that want to exploit the odd eldritch mysteries for profit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T19:40:33-07:00","id":1411040,"title":"","content":"I would like to start out by saying that Leviathan is a great game. I do not know if what I make will ever reach the magnitude of that particular fan-made marvel, but I am inspired by it. One reason I would like to make something myself is that I would like to focus more on the Spawn and the simple fact that I would just like to contribute something that someone else might want to play.<br /> <br /> My inspiration comes from the Mythos as a whole. It seems like anymore you can find lovecraft influences everywhere. Maybe instead of Mythos I should say Cosmic Horror as a whole. It's grown so considerably as a genre. The Chronicles itself is bogged down with Lovecraftian entities. The judges of Duat, the God Machine, Idigam, Shadow cults etc...<br /> <br /> Locations, locations locations... R'lyeh is definitely not a place I want the players visiting. Not directly at least. For me actually interacting with some of these places and fleshing them out takes a lot of the oomph out of them. Carcosa, R'lyeh, Sarnath, Kadath...these players are powerful because they are mysterious. Once you shine the light on the movie monster it just isn't as impactful as when it lurked at the periphery of your vision. I would like for them to be able to visit the Dreamlands, but have it differentiated from the Hedge and Arcadia. I could see getting there by chance through the hedge, but I could not see it as a realm of Arcadia. Now when it comes to a place they could go as a shelter like a hollow or bolthole...perhaps a section of R'lyeh? I also wondered what if the R'lyeh on Earth was just a portion of a greater city or world? Imagine a vast world of basalt stone labyrinths and spires with outer gods-knows-what teeming about.<br /> <br /> The most straightforward direction I can take, though not always the best route to go, would be to have a faction with subgroups that don't want the world to end, and one group that wants it to or doesn't care if it does. Maybe for the moment I should focus on our brave monsters fighting the good fight. The lucky number seems to be 5...5 groups that then join one of 5 other groups. That is certainly one way to go. I could also snub my nose at that convention and have more/less of either category or maybe have each character be unique in that they are free of these groups and can develop whatever powers or connections they feel capable of.<br /> <br /> Bloodlines perhaps? Genetic lineages with some variety due to random mutation? 5 escaped Spawn that ruled, bred, and then went somewhere. Maybe banished or maybe waiting to come back. Maybe still watching their progeny from afar or just on the other side of the mirror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T23:58:38-07:00","id":1411050,"title":"","content":"I'm new to google documents (I'm a bit of a dinosaur) but this is the very meager start I have for brainstorming.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lh1QHLM-5TYMlfn96WoMqLy9_A55aqea-psMExd8_nc/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...sMExd8_nc/edit</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T04:11:53-07:00","id":1411061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThriceHonored</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1410967-splat-pitch-long-term-hobby?p=1411040#post1411040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lucky number seems to be 5...5 groups that then join one of 5 other groups. That is certainly one way to go. I could also snub my nose at that convention and have more/less of either category or maybe have each character be unique in that they are free of these groups and can develop whatever powers or connections they feel capable of.</div> </div> </div> </div> The 5-times-5 model is common in CofD, but not universal. Look at Changeling's six Seemings and four Courts (or four other Courts, or two sets of two, and so on), and 2e Promethean's seven Lineages (one of which is &quot;unique one-offs,&quot; and then there are additional ones in post-core books) and ten Refinements.<br /> <br /> Usually, the pattern of the innate splat options (Clan, Path, Clade) is that they model archetypes of the playable <i>thing</i> (vampire-as-tempter, necromancer and alchemist, cyborg), while the social splats imply a gameplay style and focus like warfare, subterfuge, or research. The latter are more varied, though, covering social groups, decentralized philosophies, and even mindsets and urges.<br /> <br /> The current archetypes for your innate splats appear to be: medium, manipulator, warrior, prophet, shoggoth(?). So, the question is if there are any archetypes of the Deep Ones/eldritch diety/cultist that are missing, or if any of these five overlap too much to warrant separation.<br /> <br /> Then, for social splats (if you want them to be something established instead of something the PCs build)... Well, first of all, what do the Star Spawn <i>do? </i>Then, once you know that, what avenues are there to do it?<br /> <br /> Then, on a different note, are you building for 1e or 2e? In the latter case, it's worth considering what the PCs have in place of Vice and Virtue, and if their Sanity/Stability should be modelled like Morality/Integrity or more like an extra &quot;Health&quot; track like 2e Clarity or Deviant's Instability; if so they might even remove the need for a separate fuel stat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 08-30-2020, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T08:50:26-07:00","id":1411077,"title":"","content":"Also, how do you plan to separate this game from Leviathan: The Cult? It's important you are able to do this so people actually feel like giving this game a try, since the surface premise is very similar to Leviathan","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T17:59:32-07:00","id":1411447,"title":"","content":"All fair questions but the most pressing at the moment is the matter of differentiation. My initial thought would be to replace mythos as the power Stat With something like insight or cognizance. It could be because I have played too much blood-borne, but I believe I want the theme of my game to be that with understanding comes horror. I want to read that the more the human mind comes to understand the world around it The harder it will try to destroy itself. <br /> <br /> That being said I believe the following changes need to be made to my initial concept :<br /> <br /> 1) Each character should only start out with a few instinctual powers, and no rituals. <br /> <br /> 2) each character should start out at power level zero with either one alternate form or none. Their alternate bodies should be gained as their cognizance of themselves and the world of darkness around them evolves. <br /> <br /> 3) as their awareness increases they should be able to see and detect the strange, the paranormal, and the magical phenomenon around them. <br /> <br /> <br /> The game will be about learning of the monster that lives within your DNA, and all of the monsters in the world at large. Once you can see The world for what it is, you can never go back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}